 <iati-activity default-currency="EUR" hierarchy="2" humanitarian="0" iati-activities:version="2.02" xml:lang="EN" xmlns:iati-activities="http://d-portal.org/xmlns/iati-activities" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
  <iati-identifier>NL-KVK-40409352-PRJ13-132-0010</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="NL-KVK-40409352" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Netherlands Red Cross</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Localised Digital Transformation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct: RCRC national societies
Indirect: beneficiaries that these national societies serve.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In this component we work closely with National Societies to assess their current situation on the use of data and digital, and to develop a roadmap for digital transformation, with the objective to improve the speed, quality, effectiveness and accountability of the humanitarian services. From there we focus with National Societies on improving the three key areas of People, Process and Technology, by building data literacy and setting up sustainable locally led data teams (people), improving community engagement using digital messaging channels (technology), setting up safe, fast and fair cash information management systems (process, technology).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Objective 1: Improving Cash Information Management processes and tools in National Societies
Objective 2: Setting up sustainable data teams
Objective 3: National Societies have mapped where they are and want to be with their people, process and technology, and have developed and kickstarted their digital transformation roadmap.
Objective 4: Support National Societies in building their data and digital culture by providing capacity building support and implementing the use of accessible and contextual data literacy toolkits and curriculums. 
Objective 5: Embedding digital community engagement in humanitarian services of 2 national societies to use digital communication to improve the way they interact with volunteers, staff and people affected
Objective 6: Creating local Information Management tools for emergency response.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To be determined</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To improve the speed, quality and cost-effectiveness of humanitarian aid. To support the roll out of the IFRC digital transformation strategy.</narrative>
  </description>
